--- Check 3: Data directory exists ---
$ ls -ld /var/lib/pgsql/17/data
Permission denied (expected - owned by postgres, not readable by ec2-user)
Confirmed via process listing: postgres running with -D /var/lib/pgsql/17/data/

--- Check 4: pg_isready ---
$ pg_isready
bash: pg_isready: command not found
NOTE: pg_isready not in ec2-user PATH. PG binaries are at /usr/pgsql-17/bin/.
However, PG is confirmed running via systemctl and psql queries succeed.

--- Check 5: PG version ---
$ sudo -u postgres psql -t -c "SELECT version();"
